---
/* The arrow leaving a box: this link leaves the site.
 *
 * One copy for every surface that owes the reader that warning — the nav, the mobile overlay, the footer.
 * A link that steals a tab without saying so is the same small betrayal wherever it sits, so the mark is a
 * component rather than a glyph each surface remembers to paste. The sr-only line is the half of the signal
 * a glyph cannot carry: `target="_blank"` is silent to a screen reader unless the link says so itself.
 */
---

<svg class="external-icon" width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
    <path
        d="M3.5 1.5H10.5V8.5M10.5 1.5L1.5 10.5"
        stroke="currentColor"
        stroke-width="1.2"
        stroke-linecap="round"
        stroke-linejoin="round"></path>
</svg>
<span class="sr-only">(opens in a new tab)</span>

<style>
    /* `inline-block` against Tailwind's preflight, which makes every svg a block: as a block it takes a line
       of its own in any non-flex parent — which is how it first landed under the label it belongs beside. A
       flex parent blockifies it back, so this is right in both. */
    .external-icon {
        display: inline-block;
        vertical-align: middle;
        opacity: 0.4;
        flex-shrink: 0;
    }
</style>
